            "A Kaizen Event, alternatively termed a Kaizen Blitz or Rapid Improvement Event (RIE), is a structured, five-day cross-functional intervention designed to achieve breakthrough operational improvements across a specific segment of the value stream. Kaizen events are not casual brainstorming sessions; they follow a rigorous, non-negotiable five-day protocol. Day One is dedicated to team alignment, baseline data re-verification on the Gemba, and waste identification training for all participants. Day Two focuses on root-cause analysis, 5-Why problem decomposition, and spaghetti diagram mapping. Day Three represents the physical execution phase: machine guards are dismantled, equipment is physically unbolted from the concrete floor and rearranged into U-shaped continuous flow cells, shadow boards for 5S tooling are constructed, and setup times are slashed using SMED techniques. Day Four tests the new cellular flow, refines standard work combination sheets, and trains operators on line balance. Day Five culminates in executive management presentation, operational sign-off, and implementation of 30-day tracking dashboards.",
